        "comments": "The board got an 3.3V TTL as shown on the picture below. It runs on 115200 8n1.\n\n{{:media:gigaset:gigaset-604-il-serial.jpg?400}}\n\nPIN 1 and PIN 2 are aparently BOOTSELECT signals. If you short them, you can run an UART loader (useful in case you bricked the board).\n\nThe procedure is the same as described in the page of [[toh:astoria:arv7518pw|ARV7518PW]]\n<code>\nROM VER: 1.0.3                                                                                            \nCFG 04                                                                                                    \nRead EEPROMX                                                                                              \n X                                                                                                        \nUART\n</code>\n",
